 /**
+* The defensive hint appended to an ordinary (non-denial) mutation failure
+* under `self-checking`: the failure MAY be a sandbox permission issue the
+* filesystem fence could not classify. It steers to the explicit escalation
+* channel — filesystem operations have no automatic re-run unlock — and
+* demands the same deliberate self-check as the command paths: do not retry
+* unless the access is intentional.
+*/
+const SELF_CHECK_FAIL_HINT = "\n[sandbox: self-check notice — this operation failed; this may be a sandbox permission issue; unless this access is intentional, do not re-run this operation — if it IS intentional and permission-related, retry this exact operation with sandbox_permissions (the narrowest wider mode that suffices) + justification; the approval prompt asks the user]";
+/**
 * The filesystem escalation API: advertisement gating, per-call policy
 * resolution, the one-approved wider retry, and denial-marker mapping. A pure
 * product of `ctx` at plugin apply time.
@@ -1145,16 +1154,25 @@
 	* same-turn escalation hint, so a policy denial reads identically to bash's
